# ouroboros#104: a tolerance fixture whose stdout carries LABELS. The _tol
# comparator once extracted the numeric tokens only, so any non-numeric
# text (a label, a string, an error line without digits) was invisible and
# could diverge silently; it now compares the text with numbers masked and
# the numbers within tolerance. The dot below is SIMD-reassociated on the
# AOT (tolerance, not bytes), which is why this stays a _tol fixture.
a is zeros of 1000
b is zeros of 1000
i is 0
loop while i < 1000:
    a[i] is (i + 1) * 0.1
    b[i] is (1000 - i) * 0.3
    i is i + 1
print of "dot:"
print of (dot of [a, b])
print of "norm:"
print of (norm of a)
print of "done"
